			<div class="content" id="post-content-4861029">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type</strong>: SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre</strong>: Horror/Mystery</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout</strong>: Standard layout, including a picture of the watch, interviews and testing.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch</strong>: When wearing this watch, all sequences of numbers will become the Fibonacci code. All numbers change in the wearers eyes to be in the sequence of 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13 and so on. The wearer will also only be able to complete mathematic equations including the Fibonacci code. Images or paintings including faces will also turn into the face of Fibonacci.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative</strong>: The central narrative of this SCP will be revealed throughout a series of interviews and tests. The first interview is with the original owner of this SCP, now named SCP-XXXX-A. SCP-XXXX-A is a human male, approximately 1.7m in height. His personality is described as “Partially paranoid and curious.” During his interview, SCP-XXXX-A, who originally owned the watch before it was acquired by the foundation, will describe it as &quot;A comfortable item of clothing I used to wear.&quot; They will state that after purchasing it from a local garage sale in █████, they did not notice anything strange until a few days after, when they wore it for the first time. They will say that numbers in their life started to change rapidly, and he could no longer do basic equations other than those in the Fibonacci code. He will then state that when visiting an art museum with his family while wearing the watch, all self-portraits and paintings including faces turned into the face of Fibonacci. He also noted that in real life, people's faces did not change to that of Fibonacci. Finally, the man will state that after 5 consecutive days of wearing the watch, he began to become terrified of the watches power and decided to call the police. The police did not care about the man's concerns as they did not believe him, but the foundation later contained SCP-XXXX-A and SCP-XXXX during a raid of SCP-XXXX-A's house.</p>
<p>The second section of narrative will be a series of tests performed by a Dr. █████. The first test will be a test to see if the SCP can make any form of image of a face transform into Fibonacci's. A D-Class personnel will be given 3 copies of the same image. One will be a digital .png file, one will be printed onto paper and one shall be an artist's renditioning of the image. After wearing the watch for 10 minutes with the images in front of them, the D-Class will then be asked if the faces in each image changed to that of Fibonacci. The D-Class will state that yes, all faces became Fibonacci’s. The second test was conducted on a D-Class that had previously been a mathematician before being contained at Site-██. This test included the D-Class wearing the watch while solving multiple simple equations. The first 12 equations that the D-Class solved were done with general ease, however, after this point, the D-Class seemed to struggle with solving further equations. When asked why, the D-Class simply stated, “It’s Fibonacci. It’s all Fibonacci.” The third and final test was conducted using SCP-5755 (<a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5755">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-5755</a>) A D-Class personnel was given 4 images while wearing SCP-XXXX, all the images being of SCP-5755's “sources”. The D-Class is then asked to say the numbers in the sources, and gives the output, “112358, 132134, 558914, 423337”. They are then asked to shuffle the papers and once again say the numbers in the sources. The D-Class only repeats the same numbers they originally stated. These are of course the beginning numbers of the Fibonacci code in sequential order, and not the correct source numbers.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber</strong>: It's a watch that tells time in Fibonacci code, displays numbers in the Fibonacci code and overall changes the wearers mind into that of a pure follower of Fibonacci and his sequence.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes</strong>: This is a very detailed SCP, and I have done my best to include each detail that I would like to be put into the final article in this greenlighting pitch. All feedback is also welcome. Thanks!</p>
<p>THIS IS VERSION 2</p>
